    "result_text": "The full test suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 2/2 tests passing \u2014 these are the only tests in the project).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the structured address form on the create-owner endpoint (`POST /api/owners`), keeping the flat `address` accepted for backward compatibility.\n\n**Contract (`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`)**\n- Added `addressLine1` and `addressLine2` to the `OwnerFields` schema; documented `address` as the composed, normalized response value.\n- Removed `address` from the `required` list, so structured-only owners (and earlier minimal owners) still bind \u2014 validity is now enforced in code as \"either form, plus city\".\n\n**Domain / persistence**\n- `Owner.java`: added `addressLine1` / `addressLine2` columns with getters/setters.\n- Added `address_line1` / `address_line2` columns to all four `schema.sql` files (hsqldb \u2014 used by the tests \u2014 plus h2, mysql, postgres). Seed inserts use explicit column lists, so the new nullable columns are safe.\n\n**Behaviour**\n- `AddressNormalizer.compose(...)`: prefers the structured fields \u2014 normalized `addressLine1`, with a single space and normalized `addressLine2` appended when present \u2014 falling back to the normalized flat `address` when `addressLine1` is blank. Every component runs through the existing normalization (trim, collapse whitespace, upper-case, expand `ST\u2192STREET` etc.).\n- `ValidateRequiredOwnerFields` (POST): computes the effective address, rejects only when neither `addressLine1` nor flat `address` is non-blank (reported as the `address` field), normalizes the structured lines back onto the request, and stores the composed value in `address`.\n- `ApplyOwner` (PUT): applies the same composition/normalization for consistency.\n- The mapper auto-maps the same-named fields both directions, so the response returns normalized `addressLine1`/`addressLine2` and the composed `address`.\n\nThe `household hash`, `postcode validation`, and `locality` consumers read `postcode`/`city` (unchanged structured fields) and the stored composed `address`, so they now operate on the structured values when present and the flat address otherwise.\n\nThe two acceptance tests \u2014 structured normalization/composition (`addressLine1` \u2192 `10 KING STREET`, `address` equals it) and continued acceptance of the flat form \u2014 both pass.",
